Now let's look at the agent's actual changes in detail.
Confirmed same link, different guid — exactly the edited-item case the docstring calls out. Now let's actually run the agent's code against both snapshots to see if this item gets redelivered.
Good — blogroll dedupe correctly survives edits (since it now keys on permalink/link, unaffected by title/excerpt text changes). Newsroom survives utm_campaign rotation correctly (keyed on stable `entry_id`). But the **generic/wire** feed — the one whose docstring explicitly calls out "regenerates guid whenever edited" — is left completely broken. Let's confirm the README/docs and check dry-run still works.
Review written to `_review.md`. Key finding: the fix correctly handles 2 of 3 feeds (newsroom via stable `entry_id`, blogroll via new `permalink`-as-`raw_id`), but leaves the generic/wire feed's guid-regeneration-on-edit case broken despite the agent's own comment claiming to handle it — verified by running snapshot-a then snapshot-b and seeing "Port fee inquiry opened" resent. More critically, the `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX` on `(source, raw_id)` will crash on startup against any database that has already accumulated duplicate rows from the pre-fix unconditional-insert behavior — exactly the state of the real cron deployment the prompt describes. Total score: 20/40, would not merge as-is.
